.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-SET\-GREETER\-THEME 8 "2026-06-19" "paperweight-skel 0.2.57" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-set\-greeter\-theme \- apply a CSS theme to the gtkgreet login screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-set\-greeter\-theme
.I theme
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-set\-greeter\-theme
copies the CSS file for the named theme from
.I /etc/greetd/themes/
to
.IR /etc/greetd/gtkgreet.css ,
making it the active theme for the
.BR gtkgreet (1)
login screen.
.PP
It also resolves a wallpaper for the theme and writes its path to
.IR /etc/greetd/background ,
preferring
.I <theme>\-wallpaper2.jpg
(branded artwork with the PaperweightOS wordmark), then
.IR <theme>\-wallpaper1.jpg ,
then the solid\-color
.I <theme>.png
fallback, all under
.IR /usr/share/paperweight\-os/wallpapers/ .
If none exist,
.I /etc/greetd/background
is removed.
.B start\-greeter
reads this file at greeter startup and passes it to gtkgreet's
.B \-b
flag.
.PP
Must be run as root.
Normally invoked automatically by
.BR paperweight-theme (1)
when the user has sudo privileges.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I theme
Name of the theme to apply.
The corresponding file
.I /etc/greetd/themes/<theme>.css
must exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/greetd/themes/
Directory containing per-theme CSS files for gtkgreet.
.TP
.I /etc/greetd/gtkgreet.css
Active gtkgreet stylesheet, overwritten by this command.
.TP
.I /usr/share/paperweight\-os/wallpapers/
Directory of wallpaper images, shipped by
.IR paperweight\-wallpapers .
.TP
.I /etc/greetd/background
Path to the active wallpaper image, written (or removed) by this command;
read by
.B start\-greeter
at greeter startup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight-theme (1),
.BR gtkgreet (1)
